      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "Suppose $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(C)=-5,$ What is the value of $det(4C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=4$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(4C) & ={4}^{2}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-80.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
